lift_jobmods: an extra function entry may name its module (`<sha>:<addr>` in LBP_JOBMOD_EXTRA_FUNCS).

All WWS job modules load at LS 0x4000, so a bare entry is offered to every module whose code spans it. In Resistance 3
a firefight in Haven reached 0x5318 of jobmod_8f987d5458b2 through an indirect branch (~20M interpreted steps in
100 s); the same address also cut a function in jobmod_b23cc96ca61e (a loop at 0x52F0 then took two trampolines a
pass instead of a goto) and jobmod_e8edba4f27ff. The keyed form gives the entry to the module the census found it
in only; a key that names no module, or an address outside its module, stops the lift with an error.

Test: tools/test_lift_jobmods_extra_funcs.py (two synthetic modules: a bare entry splits both, a keyed one only
its module; the two errors). After the module rebuild 0x5318 starts a function in jobmod_8f987d5458b2 only.

Each module's range is the span at its own link base (module_base, #488), so a keyed entry is checked against that.

Upstream: not proposed yet.
